  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">οὐ πρὸς τυράννας ὁμιλίαν.</l>
    <l n="2" para="true">ἡ ἀνδρὸς τοῖς πλείστοις ἀγνοια.</l>
    <l n="3" para="true">πὶ πρὸς ψυχῇ ἀγαθά.]</l>
    <l n="4" type="heading" level="1" caput="2" para="true">II.</l>
    <l n="5" para="true">Substantivorum quædam Geniti-</l>
    <l n="6">vum ascisçunt, interveniente ejusdem</l>
    <l n="7">casus adjectivo, quod laudationem</l>
    <l n="8">aut vituperationem continet. ut:</l>
    <l n="9" para="true">ἀνὴρ μεγάλης ἀρετῆς.</l>
    <l n="10" para="true">ἀνθρωπῷ Ὑπυλῶτς ςόματος.</l>
    <l n="11" para="true">[<i>Observatio.</i> Quandoque tamen,</l>
    <l n="12">pro Genitivo, usurpatur Dativus; adjecti-</l>
    <l n="13">vo cum priore substantivo in casu con-</l>
    <l n="14">veniente. ut: ἀνὴρ μέγας ἀρετῇ.</l>
    <l n="15" type="heading" level="2" para="true">Regula Convenientiæ Adjectivi</l>
    <l n="16" type="heading" level="2">cum Substantivo.</l>
    <l n="17" para="true">Adjectiva cum Substantivis, quibus</l>
    <l n="18">adjiciuntur, eodem numero, genere, &amp;</l>
    <l n="19">casu, cohærent, ut:</l>
    <l n="20" para="true">καλὸς κόραξ, καλὸν ὠόν.</l>
    <l n="21" para="true">τῶν μεγάλων ἀδικημάτων μεγάλα ὑπὸ ᾱ</l>
    <l n="22">τιμωρίαν τῶν ἐξ.</l>
    <l n="23" para="true">[<i>Observationes.</i> 1. Quando duo Ad-</l>
    <l n="24">jectiva sic concurrunt, alterum fit sub-</l>
    <l n="25">stantivum. ut:</l>
    <l n="26" para="true">ἔχοντ ἐμὲ πολλοὶ φίλοι.</l>
  </main_text>
